    <title>Multiscale Implicit Stream-Power Erosion (MISE)</title>
    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><anchor id="md_docs_2content_2dev_2hydraulic__mise_1autotoc_md21"/> This document details the theory, geomorphological formulations, implicit solver, and multiscale architecture of <computeroutput>hydraulic_mise</computeroutput> in HighMap.</para>
<sect1 id="md_docs_2content_2dev_2hydraulic__mise_1autotoc_md22">
<title>1. Overview</title>
<para><computeroutput>hydraulic_mise</computeroutput> (Multiscale Implicit Stream-power Erosion) simulates long-term landscape evolution by solving coupled equations of fluvial bedrock incision, hillslope diffusion/debris flow, and alluvial sediment deposition across a dynamically re-routed drainage graph.</para>
<para><image type="html" name="../../images/hydraulic_comparison_mise.png" inline="yes"></image>
</para>
<para>Unlike explicit particle tracing or simple height filtering, MISE uses:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><bold>Implicit integration</bold>: Unconditionally stable large time steps without numerical blow-up.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Topological drainage graphs</bold>: Built using monotone priority-queue depression filling (Radix heap / bucket flood).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Coupled sediment conservation</bold>: Eroded material is carried downstream as bedload and suspended sediment until equilibrium deposition conditions are met.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Pyramidal multiscale scheduling</bold>: Macro-valleys are carved at coarse base resolutions and refined down to fine rills with domain-warped upsampling.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".mermaid"><codeline><highlight class="normal">flowchart<sp/>TD</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>A[&quot;Input<sp/>Terrain<sp/>z&quot;]<sp/>--&gt;<sp/>B[&quot;Depression<sp/>Filling<sp/>&amp;<sp/>Lake<sp/>Identification<sp/>(Priority<sp/>Flood)&quot;]</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>B<sp/>--&gt;<sp/>C[&quot;Flow<sp/>Routing<sp/>(Receivers<sp/>&amp;<sp/>Topological<sp/>Sorting)&quot;]</highlight></codeline>
