<sect1 id="md_docs_2content_2dev_2hydraulic__mise_1autotoc_md23">
<title>2. Theoretical Formulation and Kinematics</title>
<sect2 id="md_docs_2content_2dev_2hydraulic__mise_1autotoc_md24">
<title>Drainage Graph and Depression Filling</title>
<para>Surface flow routes downhill from donors to receivers. To resolve local depressions (pits, sinks, and closed lakes), the terrain is processed with a priority flood algorithm:</para>
<para><orderedlist>
<listitem><para>A boundary queue seeds the flood, tracking minimum spill elevation.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Pits are identified and tagged (<computeroutput>lake</computeroutput>), grouping flooded basins and their associated spillway outlets (<computeroutput>lake_outlet</computeroutput>).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Flow directions assign each non-outlet cell $i$ to a downslope receiver cell $r(i)$:</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para>$$P(i \to j) \propto \max\left(0, \frac{z_i - z_j}{d_{ij}}\right)^{\gamma}$$</para>
<para>where $\gamma = \text{receiver_exp}$ and $d_{ij} \in 1, \sqrt{2} </para>
</sect2>
</sect1>
